{
    "word": "futility",
    "lang_code": "en",
    "source_file_to_entries": {
        "raw-wiktextract-data.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "c3515bbb-6a92-3098-9660-658c1ea21519",
                "word": "futility",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "6eb474fb-4306-4c7b-a29f-fe64993b65f6",
                        "entry_id": "c3515bbb-6a92-3098-9660-658c1ea21519",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "futilities"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "7b4b7d79-b30f-3785-a902-b0ed077aa9ab",
                        "entry_id": "c3515bbb-6a92-3098-9660-658c1ea21519",
                        "glosses": [
                            "The quality of being futile or useless."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "uncountable",
                            "usually"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "9eea3959-d27a-46f8-ab46-f2619ada1995",
                                "sense_id": "7b4b7d79-b30f-3785-a902-b0ed077aa9ab",
                                "text": "an exercise of futility"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "fad118a4-73a0-4091-b709-c53bc4deca0d",
                                "sense_id": "7b4b7d79-b30f-3785-a902-b0ed077aa9ab",
                                "text": "His taking the bar exam for a third time was pure futility."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "4737d931-f381-45a3-a3fe-2ef0d95b607c",
                                "sense_id": "7b4b7d79-b30f-3785-a902-b0ed077aa9ab",
                                "text": "“Has my dad come?” he asked.\n“You can see he hasn’t,” said Mrs. Morel, cross with the futility of the question."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "8431d0a5-d3e5-3069-b078-be2ba74777b7",
                        "entry_id": "c3515bbb-6a92-3098-9660-658c1ea21519",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Something, especially an act, that is futile."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "countable",
                            "usually"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "b8ddcc3c-698e-4a17-a005-c9814e8ad3e3",
                                "sense_id": "8431d0a5-d3e5-3069-b078-be2ba74777b7",
                                "text": "But fashion and authority apart, and bringing Plato to the test of reason, take from him, his sophisms, futilities, and incomprehensibilities, and what remains?"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "104174be-50c2-4a19-9340-ddc39d265489",
                                "sense_id": "8431d0a5-d3e5-3069-b078-be2ba74777b7",
                                "text": "No man oppresses thee, can bid thee fetch or carry, come or go, without reason shewn. […] No man, wiser, unwiser, can make thee come or go: but thy own futilities, bewilderments, thy false appetites for Money, Windsor Georges and such like?"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "d43aa211-20a5-4c3b-8b99-45f581d8ebe8",
                                "sense_id": "8431d0a5-d3e5-3069-b078-be2ba74777b7",
                                "text": "An excessive solicitude to shield those others from one's own trials and hardships, to preserve the exact quality of the revelation, for example, had been the fruitful cause of crippling errors, spiritual tyrannies, dogmatisms, dissensions, and futilities."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "3a344cd1-4e50-409c-80e7-94ac79f1909b",
                                "sense_id": "8431d0a5-d3e5-3069-b078-be2ba74777b7",
                                "text": "But men will chatter and you and I will still shout our futilities to each other across the stage until the last silly curtain falls plump! upon our bobbing heads."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "c1e9c00c-1339-4673-955c-7ade84b99e34",
                                "sense_id": "8431d0a5-d3e5-3069-b078-be2ba74777b7",
                                "text": "There are moments of profound existential angst, howls of despair at the absurd futilities of war and a sneering disgust at the soul-destroying wastage of human potential."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "23418337-56ba-353e-8fa8-18cb44793106",
                        "entry_id": "c3515bbb-6a92-3098-9660-658c1ea21519",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Unimportance."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "uncountable",
                            "usually"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "6750f808-482b-4e0d-98bf-12ef246585a8",
                                "sense_id": "23418337-56ba-353e-8fa8-18cb44793106",
                                "text": "Her empty chatter, her futility, her childish coquetry and frivolity—such light wares could hardly be the whole substance of any woman’s being; […]"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "1532fb26-220a-4b7c-b410-c35026478911",
                        "source_entry_id": "c3515bbb-6a92-3098-9660-658c1ea21519",
